   type:"Site-specific, ephemeral installation",materials:"Unfired local clay, banana fibre, recorded audio",site:"Kueba di Indjan, Tera Kora",place:"Curaçao",lat:12.16,lon:-68.90,
   text:["Land Song was created using 100 unfired, hand-built clay globular flutes made through social collaboration with the Curaçao community; regional clay gathered from the land and processed onsite into a refined terra sigillata slip; locally sourced banana fiber gifted by the social design initiative Farm to Crafts; and an original sound composition by ‘io Kahoku Lahuikoa Luger (the artist’s son), incorporating bird calls, flute sounds and field recordings gathered throughout the island.", "kueba di indjan A limestone cave nestled within the northern plains of San Pedro, surrounded by red volcanic soil and native cacti. The cave served as a shared site for three works: Land Songs by Cannupa Hanska Luger, The Land’s Hexagonised Treasures by Avantia Damberg, and Karga (Carry, Load, Charge), a performance by Nash Caldera in collaboration with Future Organisms. Together, the works engaged with the cave’s natural environment through sound, light, and movement."],bio:["Cannupa Hanska Luger (Mandan, Hidatsa, Arikara, Lakota) is an award-winning multidisciplinary artist and cultural innovator whose expansive practice introduces new methodologies and speculative technologies rooted in Indigenous innovation. Through ceramics, installation, performance, and community engagement, he uplifts cultural continuity, ecological repair, and collective care. His work is exhibited and collected internationally."],
